 ## Menu behavior
 
+Normal builds use the following rules:
+
 | Condition | Result |
 | --- | --- |
-| Input device present | Countdown runs to the timeout |
-| No input device | `fallback_timeout` applies |
+| Nonnegative timeout | Countdown runs to `timeout`; zero selects the default immediately |
 | Negative timeout with input | Waits for a key |
 | Negative timeout without input | `fallback_timeout` applies |
-| Failed boot | Returns to the menu without a countdown |
+| Failed boot | Returns without a countdown when input exists; otherwise `fallback_timeout` applies |
 
 The menu shows the configuration source, the entry list, the injection summary and the first error.
 
+### Diagnostic firmware hold
+
+`PcdUniXNUDiagnosticMenuHold` defaults to `FALSE`. A board can explicitly enable
+it for diagnostic firmware in its DSC:
+
+```ini
+[PcdsFixedAtBuild]
+  gUniXNUPkgTokenSpaceGuid.PcdUniXNUDiagnosticMenuHold|TRUE
+```
+
+Rebuild the firmware and its boot image using the
+[UEFI integration workflow](/porting/uefi-firmware). The enabled mode displays
+`Diagnostic hold` and keeps the menu visible until an explicit selection. This
+firmware policy covers built-in and loaded configurations, the Tools submenu,
+and menu re-entry after a payload returns. A loaded `unixnu.toml` cannot override
+it through `timeout`, `fallback_timeout`, or `rotate`.
+
+The highlight does not rotate. Missing input and input errors keep the menu
+waiting. Timer or event failures cannot select an entry automatically because
+this mode uses neither timer events nor `WaitForKey`: each poll first calls
+`Stall(100000)` for a requested 100 ms delay, then checks the current `ConIn` and
+reads a key if available. A console that appears later can still accept input.
+Physical input handles are not enumerated in this mode; the initial `input` log
+field reports only whether a `ConIn` callback is available.
+Existing navigation and explicit selection keys retain their behavior, including
+the ability to choose XNU, Tools, Return to firmware, Restart, or Power off.
+Escape alone does not exit the menu.
+
+The older `PcdUniXNUBuiltinMenuWaitForInput` only changes built-in configuration
+settings and retains the normal fallback timeout when input is absent. Use the
+diagnostic hold PCD when an unattended diagnostic menu must remain visible.
+
+Host tests exercise the actual menu loop with simulated firmware services.
+Physical input and real delay timing remain unverified until a device test.
+The mode depends on working `Stall` and `ReadKeyStroke` implementations; it does
+not change confirmation dialogs or a tool plugin's internal loop. If no input
+works, use the device's physical reset and bootloader recovery procedure.
+
